                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.12155/150: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-08-17T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 17,
                                1925—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>183. Your 154, August 13, 9 a.m. In view of reported attitude of Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs Department desires you in your discretion either to bring matter
                    to personal attention of President or to request Foreign Minister to take such
                    action. Emphasis should be placed upon recent losses on both sides of border due
                    to floods and upon urgent necessity for contemplated works to prevent recurrence
                    such damages.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
